date-released: 2026-09-19
keywords:
  - AI transparency
  - training data disclosure
  - signed observations
  - Merkle seals
  - OpenTimestamps
  - Ed25519
abstract: >
  The Crovia Substrate records observations of what AI providers publish about their
  training data as Ed25519-signed envelopes in an append-only AXIOM ledger, Merkle-seals the
  ledger hourly and anchors new roots in Bitcoin through OpenTimestamps. This repository
  holds the collectors, the observer, the sealer, the anchoring job and the Phase-0
  post-processors that enforce the canonical definitions of every headline figure. Live
  observation of absence has moved to TACET (croviatrust/countersign); the ledger built here
  is preserved as the 2026 archive.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "TACET: Verifiable Silence for AI Training Disclosure"
    url: https://github.com/croviatrust/countersign
